desc(
	mode: "source"
	language: "general"
	title: "Template Var Unescaped With Safeseq"
	title_zh: "检测到Template Var Unescaped With Safeseq",
	type: vuln
	level: middle
	rule_id: "source-insecure-api-template-var-unescaped-with-safeseq"
	risk: "xss"
	desc: <<<DESC
Migrated from Semgrep rule `template-var-unescaped-with-safeseq` (/tmp/semgrep-rules/python/django/security/audit/xss/template-var-unescaped-with-safeseq.yaml).
Original message: Detected a template variable where autoescaping is explicitly disabled with '| safeseq' filter. This allows rendering of raw HTML in this segment. Ensure no user data is rendered here, otherwise this is a cross-site scripting (XSS) vulnerability. If you must do this, use `mark_safe` in your Python code.

CWE: CWE-79: Improper Neutralization of Input During Web Page Generation ('Cross-site Scripting')
References:
- https://docs.djangoproject.com/en/3.0/ref/templates/builtins/#safeseq
DESC
	solution: <<<SOLUTION
Review the flagged code and follow the framework's secure coding guidance: use safe APIs, escape output, and avoid hardcoded credentials.
SOLUTION
	alert_min: 1
	"file://pos.html": <<<POS
{{,[<jxt'Z|	
 
	  	
 	safeseq

POS
	"safefile://neg.sample": <<<NEG
# safe sample
no secrets here
just regular code
NEG
)

${*.html}.pattern_regex(/{{.*?\|\s+safeseq(\s+}})?/) as $p0
$p0 as $hit
alert $hit for {
	level: "middle",
	title: "Template Var Unescaped With Safeseq",
	title_zh: "检测到Template Var Unescaped With Safeseq",
	message: "Template Var Unescaped With Safeseq",
}
